{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01W7sJfUTK52ZMnEVmfpJ1T6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 33 tests pass. The changes enhance R4.3 compliance by making the verification helpers explicitly check link type:\n\n- `verifyHardLink` now uses `os.Lstat` (instead of `os.Stat`) and verifies the link does NOT have `os.ModeSymlink` set before checking inode identity via `os.SameFile`.\n- `verifySymlink` now uses `os.Lstat` to verify the file IS a symlink (`os.ModeSymlink` is set) before checking the readlink target.\n\nThese checks run on every test that calls either helper, covering hard link creation, symlink creation, force overwrite, backup, verbose, multi-target, relative symlink, and no-dereference scenarios — matching R4.3's requirement that tests verify both correct target and correct link type."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1553,"cache_read_input_tokens":38404,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1553},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"98ea77eb-b7d0-4a95-bbef-0c4dc388563d","uuid":"c66a673d-cc14-4437-9199-238158e260bc"}
